    "name": "Effect: Mind Doubling Mutagen (Moderate)",
    "type": "effect",
    "system": {
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>Granted by @UUID[Compendium.marquiste-additions.corpsecaps-cauldron.Item.Yiixd2oa6lbgHtfU]</p><p><strong>Benefit</strong> You gain a +2 item bonus to Perception checks and Intelligence-based skill checks (Arcana, Crafting, Lore, Occultism, and Society), and a +2 item bonus to saving throws against mental and emotion effects. You gain access to the Co-ordinated Thinking action, described below.</p><p><strong>Drawback</strong> The two brains can interact poorly when handing off control of the body, giving you a –1 item penalty to Dexterity-based skill checks and a –2 item penalty to Reflex saves. Mental damage hits you harder, as your increased brain capacity has more to lose, giving you weakness 5 to mental damage.</p><p><strong>Mutant Innervation</strong> If you have the Mutant Innervation feat, your brains have become adept at working together to fend off mental attacks. Whenever you attempt a saving throw against a mental effect, roll twice and take the better of the two results. This is a fortune effect.</p>"
        },
